rofit pool.","It accounts for 0.1% of sector revenue and 0.3% of sector operating profit.","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.04 across 219 companies in the universe; the top four hold 25% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted lower, down 16% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 24% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 35% and a beta of 1.08, it moves roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.62 vs 5y 1.10), so read it loosely.","About $71.0M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 54% in the 2020 crash, 38% in the 2022 bear market and 62% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $175 (margin of safety -6%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 53%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $133 to $232 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Basic Materials peers: EV/EBITDA 10.8 vs 8.5 and P/FCF 28.6 vs 22.8 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 6% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 3.5% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 8.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 10 covering analysts target $193 on average, 4% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 21% clears the cost of capital of 8.6% by 13pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.31).","It runs a 24% gross margin and converts 9% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.45x.","ROE of 29% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.6x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.9x net debt to EBITDA ($297.9M of cash against $1.8B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 12.7x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.3, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 3.66)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 2.4% over 3 years, 7.3% over 5 years and 7.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 21.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -19.6% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex runs 2.5x depreciation (18.1% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 15, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 2.9% on average."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.3%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 7.3% a year to shareholders (6.8% in buybacks and 0.5% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 5.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 30 consecutive years, raising it 50.7% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 2,800 employees, each generates about $825K of revenue, 1.3x the Basic Materials median, and productivity has risen 10.6% a year.","That works out to $71K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.2M (4x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $8K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":61,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $149.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 54, gates 15/25)","ROIC 21.4% vs WACC 8.6%","Revenue grew 7.3%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone","Returns 7.3% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 6% above fair value of $175","EV/EBITDA 10.8x vs sector 8.5x","P/FCF 28.6x vs sector 22.8x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":148.78,"vc":{"base":175.03,"base_src":"dcf","bear":133.17,"bull":231.